ef=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T19:02:38-07:00","id":1466217,"title":"","content":"For myself Guide to the Sabbat is the most robust 'chassis' to hang other parts off of, theres not much on TSOC that I could see myself using that isn't better done in LHROOH.<br /> <br /> I tend more towards the treatment of Paths in GttS than in FP, but thats not to say FP is bad.<br /> <br /> Hell, there's better quality of writing in the majority of the SV releases than in the vast majority of the official V5 releases I've read.<br /> <br /> I also recommend ( <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374123/V5-Bloodlines-Unbound-Volume-1?src=newest_community&amp;filters=45622_45624_45645\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/pr...22_45624_45645</a> ) for additional info and consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T13:00:50-08:00","id":1467097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466095-sabbat-fanmade-book-reviews-brainstorming-to-fuse-different-ideas-from-those-books?p=1466217#post1466217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For myself Guide to the Sabbat is the most robust 'chassis' to hang other parts off of, theres not much on TSOC that I could see myself using that isn't better done in LHROOH.<br /> <br /> I tend more towards the treatment of Paths in GttS than in FP, but thats not to say FP is bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the lead author on Guide to the Sabbat:<br /> 1) Very happy to hear you liked the book.<br /> 2) Our intent was very much to write a framework from which players and storytellers could develop their stories. Given that the Sabbat is in something of a state of flux, there seemed little sense in trying to pin it down canonically. There are different things to like in each interpretation of the Sabbat, so our intent was to largely leave that to preference.<br /> <br /> That said, I am currently working on our follow-up guide to the Gehenna Fronts, which is necessitating a bit more research and establishing of 'canon'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T18:06:10-08:00","id":1467137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466095-sabbat-fanmade-book-reviews-brainstorming-to-fuse-different-ideas-from-those-books?p=1467097#post1467097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As the lead author on Guide to the Sabbat:<br /> 1) Very happy to hear you liked the book.<br /> 2) Our intent was very much to write a framework from which players and storytellers could develop their stories. Given that the Sabbat is in something of a state of flux, there seemed little sense in trying to pin it down canonically. There are different things to like in each interpretation of the Sabbat, so our intent was to largely leave that to preference.<br /> <br /> That said, I am currently working on our follow-up guide to the Gehenna Fronts, which is necessitating a bit more research and establishing of 'canon'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Can New Orleans be a Sabbat city in the new canon?? :-)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T18:32:19-08:00","id":1467622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466095-sabbat-fanmade-book-reviews-brainstorming-to-fuse-different-ideas-from-those-books?p=1467137#post1467137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh! Can New Orleans be a Sabbat city in the new canon?? :-)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I sadly can't make any promises, just yet. We're still early doors, about 80 pages of manuscript so far, and we haven't entirely settled on the Warfronts we're going to cover. That said never say never, I had an ST run a wonderful game for us set in New Orleans so it's got some great VTM associated memories for me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STV Author - <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374164/Guide-to-the-Sabbat?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45624_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Guide to the Sabbat</a> <br /> Current Project(s): Tales from the Fronts - A Guide to the Gehenna War","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25061-karos","name":"Karos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25061_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}